course: dictionary
lesson: 5391
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning in turn, so you must pick the one that fits the sentence. «Knuckle» can mean a joint of your hand, a joint of meat, or part of a phrase. The words around it tell you which.
explain: «Count the knuckles and the gaps between them on your fist» is about the joints of your hand, because you can see them on your fist. But in «knuckle down», the word means something different: it is a phrase meaning to start working hard. Look at the words next to the word, not just the word on its own.
explain: Phrases change the meaning. «Knuckle under» means to give in and obey, so you cannot work out its meaning from the single word knuckle. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A knuckle is one of the joints of your fingers, especially where they join the hand.
fact: A knuckle can also be a joint of meat from an animal's leg, as in pork knuckle.
fact: «Knuckle down» means to start working hard.
fact: «Knuckle under» means to give in and obey.
fact: In the knuckle trick, «knuckle months have 31 days, and dip months fewer.»
exercise: «In the knuckle trick, months that land on a knuckle have 31 days.» What does knuckle mean here? | *The bumps on your closed fist | A cheap sort of meat | A dip in the ground | A sharp tool
exercise: Dad says, «Stop mucking about and knuckle down.» What does knuckle down mean? | *Start working hard | Give in and obey | Hit the table with your fist | Crack your fingers
exercise: Nora's teacher says, «Pork knuckle is served with potatoes.» What is a pork knuckle? | A ball of wool | A joint of your fingers | A small telling-off | *A joint of meat from an animal's leg
test: «The rules were clear, so Sam had to knuckle under and obey.» What does knuckle under mean? | *To give in and obey | Count the days in a month | Crack a joint loudly | Start working hard
test: Ben's teacher gave him a rap on the knuckles for talking. What does rap on the knuckles mean? | *A small telling-off | A knock on the door | A fight with fists | A big prize
exam: «Mia cracked her knuckles before the test.» In this sentence, knuckles means | Hard work | Months of the year | *Joints of your fingers | Joints of meat
